  %% IDEA: for personnel, the "contract" is an authorized position with a valid appointment, and the "delivery" is attendance and service. The amount is fixed by law (salary grade and step), not by a bid. The main control is the list of positions kept by DBM.
  %% SOURCES: monthly update of the plantilla of personnel in GMIS with an encoder and two approvers, personnel budget based on filled positions, Miscellaneous Personnel Benefits Fund for unfilled and new positions, Pension and Gratuity Fund, BP Forms 204 and 205 [GMIS][NBM156]. Allotment for filled positions through the GAA as allotment order, retirement and life insurance premiums by GARO, special purpose funds by SARO, Advice for use of PS Allotment [NBC599]. Tax Remittance Advice [NBC599]. Planned National Government HR and Payroll System [SFA6].
  %% GENERAL KNOWLEDGE, NOT OPENED IN A SOURCE HERE: step 1 (the document by which DBM approves positions), steps 5 to 7 (appointment and attestation by the Civil Service Commission), steps 8 to 14 (attendance record, payroll preparation, vouchers, payment through the bank), the list of deductions and receiving bodies in step 15.
